front_page(doc,'ABSTRACT',["TwinHealth AI is a local-first web platform designed to support structured multi-disease clinical risk assessment and lifestyle-care planning. The system accepts demographic, vital-sign and laboratory inputs, evaluates the availability of required features, and runs separate machine-learning pipelines for diabetes, heart disease, chronic kidney disease, liver disease and stroke risk. It presents risk estimates with explanatory factors and marks outputs as insufficient when mandatory evidence is unavailable. The application is intended as a clinical decision-support demonstration; it does not diagnose a condition. Clinical testing is required for diagnosis.", "The platform provides separate clinician and patient views. The clinician workflow captures assessment data, produces a persistent risk summary and creates a reviewable care-plan draft. The patient workflow presents date-aware activities and records task completion. Local persistence uses atomic JSON writes and a lock to reduce corruption during concurrent activity. The report describes requirements, architecture, implementation, data preparation, model integration, test strategy, limitations and future improvements. Any empirical performance values, deployment approvals and user-study observations must be entered after project evaluation.", "Keywords: clinical decision support, machine learning, chronic disease risk, FastAPI, explainable risk reporting, lifestyle adherence."]); page(doc)
